  "model_claims": [
   {
    "id": "C1",
    "text": "The previous implementation of Segment._split_cells produced incorrect splits for multi\u2011cell characters, e.g., splitting resulted in ('\ud83e\udd8a\ud83e\udd8a ', ' abcdef') instead of ('\ud83e\udd8a ', ' abcdef').",
    "source_quote": "This overshot for multi-cell characters (emoji, CJK) because it assumed all characters have equal width. The fallback loop then couldn't recover correctly, producing wrong splits like `('\ud83e\udd8a\ud83e\udd8a ', ' abcdef')` instead of `('\ud83e\udd8a ', ' abcdef')`.",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "differs"
   },
   {
    "id": "C2",
    "text": "After the fix, Segment._split_cells uses a linear scan that accumulates real cell widths and stops precisely at the cut point, yielding correct splits for multi\u2011cell characters.",
    "source_quote": "Fixed by replacing the heuristic + loop with a simple linear scan that accumulates real cell widths character by character, stopping precisely at the cut point.",
    "testable": true,
    "expect": "differs"
   }
  ],
